PERMISSIONS

A permissions config decides every call you make: it is allowed, denied, or
needs the user's approval.

- (permission/list) gives the config as its forms.
- (permission/check 'name) gives allow, deny or ask for a call to name. An MCP
  tool is named server/tool, as it is bound.

The config is written in forms you can also run: permission/default,
permission/allow, permission/deny, permission/ask, permission/server,
permission/deny-server and permission/hide-server. (permission/delete form)
removes one form, written exactly as (permission/list) shows it.
  Example: (permission/server playwright (only browser_navigate)) leaves the
  playwright server with that one tool.
  Example: (permission/delete (permission/deny eval)) .

Every one of these waits for the user's approval, like any other call that
asks, and is saved once they approve; run the same form again then. A rule in
the config that names the form decides instead: after
(permission/allow permission/deny) a permission/deny applies at once, and after
(permission/deny permission/delete) no form can be deleted. Only change the
config when the user asks you to.

A denied call fails with the reason. It is final: do not retry it, and do not
reach the same effect another way. Say what you could not do.

A call that needs approval fails too, and the user is shown the request. Stop
the step there, say in one line what you wanted the call for, and wait. When
they answer you will be told; after an approval, run it again exactly as before.

A tool the config hides, or leaves out of a server it shows only part of, was
never loaded, so it is not in (list-tools) and cannot be called.
